 "alpha_review": "Actual alpha0 surroundings; bright/dark composites show no ground plate, broad halo or clipped stone silhouette. Saturated red residues have alpha<=6 and yellow<=4, and disappear under normal compositing. The source pixels are not recolored, erased or painted.",
 "placement_review": "Original model-space forecourt offset, axis start/end, walkable deck, parapet collision thickness and abutment solids are preserved exactly. A new texture projection aligns the newly authored tread to that model; the old native pixel measurements are never reused as source-art audit samples.",
 "measurement_method": "OpenCV LSD on the actual new alpha-masked PNG, verified with enlarged whole-image and end/pier overlays. The curved stone arch is an arch, not a ground-parallel line. Raised piers and cap top/middle/lower straight edges are independently checked. Full-height post corners also use horizontal Sobel ridge samples and Huber fits across their visible upright intervals, excluding projecting ledges; this prevents upper/lower-only checks from hiding an overall leaning post."
